-- CONTROL for #1072: the MIRROR of main.mdk.  Exactly one variable is flipped -- WHICH
-- MODULE holds which impl.  c.mdk holds the site AND the SPECIFIC impl; d.mdk holds the
-- GENERAL one.  Everything else (module topology, import closure shape, the site, the
-- receiver type, the interface) is identical to main.mdk's arrangement.
--
-- This must print `specific`, and that is what turns main.mdk's `general` from "an
-- arbitrary expectation" into "most-specific-wins is decided by MODULE ORDER".
import c.{callC}
import d

main = println callC
